{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795095130,"nonce":"KwbrF+djyp+JaYm3BF8VYFZNC5w=","title":"Warn at startup when default_resources sets cpu but no memory","message":"Follow-up to e8b5967 (2026-11-19). A cluster with a require-resource-limits policy (Kyverno) refuses any container without requests.cpu, requests.memory and limits.memory. Scarab's own helpers now carry all three, but the step container and debug shell get them only from the step or the configured default_resources, and only when both axes are set. Owner decision: no built-in defaults for user containers. Log a warning at server startup when default_resources sets cpu but no memory (or memory without a limit), naming the missing field, so the refusal is not a surprise.","files":null}]}